Z||000032||Toddster||06-11-2001||05:45 PM||||Slammed, The main advantage of the Miata, as with most cars with winning traditions, is weight.<P>The Miata is the re-incarnation of the Morris Mini. when it first came out it was a laughing stock. But its low center of gravity and light weight overcame its rubberband engine shortcomings. It went on to dominate the racing circuit for years.<P>If the Fiero was just 500 pounds lighter it would have a VERY different reputation today.||||reg||1
Z||000033||Slammed Fiero||06-11-2001||06:37 PM||||The Mini?? The miata is a rear drive car , the mini is a front drive car. The Miata is closer to a bug eyed sprite, or other british original sports cars. I think it's closest relative is the Lotus Elan.<P>I believe even the maiata has put on a bit of weight since it's introduction.<P>Original Fiero's 84's weighted the same as the miata , about 2400lbs and had around the same Hp 116hp for the 1.6 miata.<P>JM||||reg||1
