Z||000035||Tryxalon||06-11-2001||08:43 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> <B> ===============<P>Now, regarding the gentleman with the 6 digit income comment...TOADSTOOL...errr I mean...Tryxalon      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> FYI bought my house last November...paid for in full...no mortgage!<BR>It is all about one's hobbies and passions.  Most of us here, the Fiero, no matter what it may cost us and/or whether we are rich and/or poor; smart as a whip and/or dumb as a box of rocks!  Boils down to choice.<P><BR>How well are you doin!?!?!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, there was much more in there, and similar comments from other Flamers. <P>To all of you: My comment was based on the majority of individuals here who have admitted a somewhat less sterling financial expertise than this individual represents.  <P>However, there is one very telling comment <I> It boils down to choice. </I> <P> This was used in defense of that individual's sense of self worth (that they perhaps correctly assumed I had impugned) and I am sure several other people were equally defensive about. <P>So, if you like it and I don't you are right and I am wrong??  <P>That is exactly what the post that I was responding to had said. <P>The expressed opinion that "anyone who disagrees with me is (insert insult here)" is obviously made by someone who has a lack of understanding, or an insufficient ego. Thus the responses I received. <P>My comment concerning lack of a 6 figure income was MEANT to tick someone off to gain their attention. I used this method since the poster I was responding to was being "willfully ignorant". <P>The point I was making was exactly the point You are making: I cannot equitably judge your choices, nor can you judge mine. Each side is an opinion that will be born out over time: in this case in the Automotive Market. Until the differences between our opinions are resolved in that marketplace, both you and I are entitled to our opinion, and to our opinion of the other person's opinion. Example being that Pontiac is no longer producing either a 2 seat or midengined vehicle and is producing and selling several Van/Suv/Crossover things. As many Azteks on the road as PT Cruisers - another vehicle they are selling as many as they make.  <P><BR>At any rate to the specific individual I quoted: You appear to be a quite successful individual and therefore excluded from my accusatory comment, hmm? <P> Thank you for your concern. I am doing quite well, thank you through the Miracle of Compounded Interest and the ever climbing Stock Market over the past 25 years. That and a minor compensation package for 20 years government service.  I am sufficiently "well off" so I may have a hobby based on a 15 year old discontinued automobile. <P>That doesn't mean I'm going to sink enough money to buy a Miata into that "toy" though - or that I won't laugh at anyone who does!!!!  <P><p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 06-11-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000036||Pontiaddict||06-11-2001||09:40 PM||||As far as D/C ripping off vehcles.<BR>The Viper is admittedly based from a 1964 shelby daytona coupe (Yes, I know shelby affiliated himself with Dodge in the 80's and 90's)<BR>The Chrisler Cirrus convertable copied the Camaro in 1994, and then again after Chevy changed the front sheetmetal in '98 <BR>The Prowler and PT Cruiser are kind of obvious, though they could be considered designed after Old Dodge and Desoto vehicles.<BR>They keep making the Neon Look more bugeyed like a Beetle<BR>Deimeler Benz had planned to strip down the Dodge Corp.'s linup before they bought them. They just didn't tell Dodge until afterwards. Would you? Expect more models to drop soon.||||reg||1
Z||000037||fyerstarter||06-11-2001||10:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tryxalon:<BR><B>All of you are, of course, entitled to your opinion. <P>However, none of you have admitted to 6 digit incomes so you cannot be THAT smart. <P>I also note that you all drive Fieros, ergo none of you are enamored with newer cars enough to give up your Fiero. <P>Ever think that is why there are so many different makes and models? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I don't make 100,000 a year but I do make over 50. I will turn 21 in a week and have no college education. For those of you thinking "Daddy got him a job in his big company" ..wrong. 3 years ago I was working at Big O Tires for $5 an hour. I am completely self taught in the field in which I work. Sorry I just had to toot my own horn just a little  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> *toot*<P>Anyway from what I can tell there are lots of successfull people on this board not just financially but otherwise. There are people who know everything about computers, or mechanics, sucessfull business people, etc.<BR> <BR>Your post sounded to me like you were trying to imply that Fieros are for poor, or stupid people. Or people who would rather have a Ferrari but the Fiero is the next best thing. ||||reg||1
